"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. The team expanded by adding five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with onboarding on September 10th. A call for ideas regarding AI-enhanced data visualization was issued, with proposals due by July 20th. The project celebrated the completion of its testing phase on October 10th. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. Recent updates include finalizing technical documentation, scheduling a steering committee meeting, and preparing for a showcase event. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, will be updated starting January next year. Additionally, a $15,000 budget has been approved for specialized training for the coding team and project managers, starting next month."
